See \code{\link{centrality_beta_measure}}.}

\item{ninl_order}{Nonnegative NINL iteration count, default three.}

\item{ninl_radius}{NINL hop radius, NULL for ceiling of mean path length.
See \code{\link{centrality_ninl}} for disconnected graphs and overrides.}

\item{map_flow}{Map equation flow model, unrecorded (default) or recorded.}

\item{map_convention}{Map equation coding convention, paper (default) or
infomap. See \code{\link{centrality_map_equation}}.}

\item{sr_prior}{SpectralRank diagonal prior, default zero; scalar or one
value per node. See \code{\link{centrality_spectralrank}}.}

\item{mcgm_radius}{MCGM hop cutoff, default two; NULL includes all reachable nodes.}

\item{mcgm_alpha}{MCGM coefficient, NULL for the published adaptive rule.
See \code{\link{centrality_mcgm}} for disconnected-graph conventions.}

\item{dkgm_radius}{DKGM hop cutoff, default two as in the paper's printed
example; NULL or infinity includes all reachable nodes and "auto"
applies the paper's half-mean-distance rule with cograph rounding.
See \code{\link{centrality_dkgm}}.}

\item{nd_order}{Steps of neighbors summed by \code{"neighbor_distance"},
a nonnegative whole number, default two; zero returns \code{nd_mass}.
See \code{\link{centrality_neighbor_distance}}.}

\item{nd_decay}{Per-step decay for \code{"neighbor_distance"}, a finite
number, default 0.2 as in the source.}

\item{nd_mass}{Benchmark centrality summed by
\code{"neighbor_distance"}: degree (default) or coreness.}

\item{ira_mass}{Node centrality allocated by \code{"ira"} and
\code{"iira"}: coreness (default, the k-shell index both sources use in
their worked examples) or degree. See \code{\link{centrality_ira}}.}

\item{ira_alpha}{Exponent on the \code{"ira"} mass, a finite number,
default one as in the source.}

\item{ira_tol}{Stopping tolerance for \code{"ira"} on the largest
absolute change between iterates, a positive finite number, default
\code{1e-6} as in the source.}

\item{ira_max_iter}{Iteration bound for \code{"ira"}, a whole number of
at least one, default 1000. Reaching it raises a
\code{cograph_no_converge} warning, which always happens on a bipartite
component with unequal vertex classes. See \code{\link{centrality_ira}}.}

\item{iira_beta}{Spreading rate for \code{"iira"}, a number in
\eqn{(0,1]}, default 0.2 as in the source.}

\item{iira_steps}{Iterations for \code{"iira"}, a nonnegative whole
number, default 50 as in the source; zero returns the initial unit
resource. See \code{\link{centrality_iira}}.}

\item{hcc_delta}{Weight on a node's own degree in the extended degree
used by \code{"hcc"} and \code{"ehcc"}, a single number in
\eqn{[0,1]}, default 0.5 as in the source. A value of one gives the
classical degree and zero drops the node's own degree. Values outside
\eqn{[0,1]} raise an error. See \code{\link{centrality_hcc}}.}

\item{lhc_radius}{Radius of the ball \eqn{\Phi(v)}{Phi(v)} summed over by
\code{"lhc"}, the \eqn{d} of the source's equation (1); a single whole
number of at least one, default 2 as in the source, which reports 2-3
as optimal. At one the ball contains only the neighbors. At or above the
diameter the score no longer changes. Values below one and non-integers
raise an error. See \code{\link{centrality_lhc}}.}

\item{ink_alpha}{Exponent \eqn{\alpha}{alpha} on each neighbor's core
number in \code{"ink"}; a single finite nonnegative number, default 1
as in the source's experiments. Zero gives the degree and one the sum
of the neighbors' core numbers. Negative values raise an error. See
\code{\link{centrality_ink}}.}

\item{nwrank_alpha}{Weight of the degree term in the shares of
\code{"nwrank"}, a single number in \eqn{[0,1]}, default 0.5 as in the
source. The link betweenness term has weight one minus this. See
\code{\link{centrality_nwrank}}.}

\item{brw_alpha}{Weight of the degree term in the move probabilities of
\code{"biased_random_walk"}, a single number in \eqn{[0,1]}, default
0.5 as in the source. See \code{\link{centrality_biased_random_walk}}.}

\item{brw_jump}{Probability that the walker of
\code{"biased_random_walk"} jumps to a uniformly chosen node, a single
number in \eqn{(0,1]}, default 0.15 as in the source.}

\item{gin_alpha}{Weight of the node's own degree in the exponent of
\code{"gin"}, a single finite nonnegative number, default 1 as in the
source. See \code{\link{centrality_gin}}.}

\item{gli_radius}{Distance range \eqn{r} summed over by \code{"gli"}, a
single whole number of at least one, default 3 as in the source. See
\code{\link{centrality_gli}}.}

\item{density_radius}{Largest distance summed over by
\code{"density_centrality"}: a single whole number of at least one,
or \code{Inf}; default 3. See
\code{\link{centrality_density_centrality}}.}

\item{sp_radius}{Largest distance summed over by
\code{"spreading_probability"}: a single whole number of at least
one, or \code{Inf}; default 3 as in the source. See
\code{\link{centrality_spreading_probability}}.}

\item{niccm_layers}{Number of layers a node contributes over in
\code{"niccm"}: a single whole number of at least one, or \code{Inf};
default 2 as in the source. See \code{\link{centrality_niccm}}.}

\item{coc_alpha}{Exponent of the distance in
\code{"correlation_centrality"}, a single finite nonnegative number,
default 3 as in the source. See
\code{\link{centrality_correlation_centrality}}.}

\item{lsc_alpha}{Weight of the neighborhood size against the clustering
sum in \code{"lsc"}, a single number between 0 and 1; default 0.2, the
value the source fixes for its experiments. See
\code{\link{centrality_lsc}}.}

\item{cn_weights}{Weights of the four classes of neighbors in
\code{"classified_neighbors"}: higher shell, same shell removed at the
same step or later, same shell removed earlier, lower shell. Four
finite nonnegative numbers. See
\code{\link{centrality_classified_neighbors}}.}

\item{hc_p}{Spreading probability of \code{"hybrid_degree"}, a single
number between 0 and 1. It has no default: without it the measure warns
and returns \code{NA}. See \code{\link{centrality_hybrid_degree}}.}

\item{hc_alpha}{Scale of the degree term in \code{"hybrid_degree"}, a
single nonnegative number; default 1000 as in the source.}

\item{hc_beta}{Balance of the degree term in \code{"hybrid_degree"}, a
single finite number; default 0.1.}

\item{topsis_attribute}{Third attribute of \code{"topsis"}, next to
degree and closeness: \code{"betweenness"} (default) or
\code{"eigenvector"}. See \code{\link{centrality_topsis}}.}

\item{topsis_weights}{Weights of degree, closeness and the third
attribute in \code{"topsis"}: three finite nonnegative numbers, default
one third each.}

\item{ei_alpha}{Weight of the friend count in the direct influence of
\code{"entropy_influence"}, a single number between 0 and 1; default 0.4
as in the source. See \code{\link{centrality_entropy_influence}}.}

\item{ei_omega}{Weight of the direct influence in
\code{"entropy_influence"}, a single number between 0 and 1; default 0.6
as in the source.}

\item{evidence_omega}{The constant \eqn{\omega}{omega} of
\code{"multi_evidence"}, a single number above 0 and at most 1; default
1 as in the source. See \code{\link{centrality_multi_evidence}}.}

\item{ksh_mu}{Weight of the neighbor's degree in \code{"ksh"} and
\code{"eskh"}, a single number between 0 and 1; default 0.4, the value
of the source's worked example (its authors tune it per network). See
\code{\link{centrality_ksh}}.}

\item{ksh_radius}{Largest distance summed over by \code{"ksh"},
\code{"eskh"}, \code{"ikh"} and \code{"eikh"}: a single whole number of
at least one, default 3 as in the sources; \code{Inf} is accepted by
\code{"ksh"} and \code{"eskh"} only. See \code{\link{centrality_ikh}}.}

\item{wdc_alpha}{Exponent of the degree in \code{"wdc"} and of the score
in \code{"ewdc"}: \code{NULL} (default) for the absolute degree
assortativity of the network, as in the source, or a single finite
nonnegative number. See \code{\link{centrality_wdc}}.}

\item{ahp_weights}{Weights of degree, betweenness and closeness in
\code{"ahp"}: three finite nonnegative numbers, not all zero, used as
given; default one third each. See \code{\link{centrality_ahp}}.}

\item{semi_ia_radius}{Largest distance summed over by \code{"semi_ia"}:
\code{NULL} (default) for 3 below 1000 nodes and 5 from there on, as in
the source, a whole number of at least one, or \code{Inf}. See
\code{\link{centrality_semi_ia}}.}

\item{semi_ia_gamma}{Exponent of the number of shortest paths in
\code{"semi_ia"}, a single number between 0 and 1; default 0.2 as in
the source.}

\item{semi_ia_max_iter}{Iteration bound of \code{"semi_ia"}, a whole
number of at least one, default 10000. Reaching it raises a
\code{cograph_no_converge} warning.}

\item{ia_steps}{Number of steps of the self-avoiding walks of
\code{"inward_accessibility"}, a whole number of at least one. It has
no default: without it the measure warns and returns \code{NA}. See
\code{\link{centrality_inward_accessibility}}.}

\item{ia_stuck}{What \code{"inward_accessibility"} does with a walk
that has no unvisited neighbor: \code{"vanish"} (default) removes
it, \code{"stay"} keeps it at its last node.}

\item{ie_beta}{Exponent of the neighbor degree in
\code{"improved_entropy"}, a single finite number; default 2 as in the
source. See \code{\link{centrality_improved_entropy}}.}

\item{physarum_steps}{Number of updates of \code{"physarum_spreader"},
a whole number of at least one. It has no default, because the source
gives no stopping rule: without it the measure warns and returns
\code{NA}. See \code{\link{centrality_physarum_spreader}}.}

\item{ar_references}{Number of references of each node in
\code{"articlerank"}: \code{NULL} (default) for the out-degree, or one
finite nonnegative number per node, in node order or named by node. See
\code{\link{centrality_articlerank}}.}

\item{entropy_gravity_radius}{Largest distance summed over by
\code{"entropy_gravity"}, a whole number of at least one or \code{Inf};
default 3 as in the source. See \code{\link{centrality_entropy_gravity}}.}

\item{ehc_p, ehc_r}{The parameters \eqn{p}, in \eqn{(0, 1]}, and \eqn{r},
above 0, of \code{"ehc"}; defaults 0.8 and 100 as in the source. See
\code{\link{centrality_ehc}}.}

\item{wnc_benchmark}{Benchmark centrality of
\code{"weight_neighborhood"}: \code{"degree"} (default) or
\code{"coreness"}. See \code{\link{centrality_weight_neighborhood}}.}

\item{wnc_alpha}{Exponent of the edge importance in
\code{"weight_neighborhood"}, a single finite number; default 1 as in
the source.}

\item{rcfb_epsilon}{Conductance \eqn{\varepsilon}{epsilon} of the links
to the virtual target in \code{"rcfb"}: 0 (default) for the limit
\eqn{\varepsilon \to 0}{epsilon -> 0}, or a positive number below the
bound of the source's equation (14). See \code{\link{centrality_rcfb}}.}

\item{wksd_alpha, wksd_mu}{The weights of the degree and of the k-shell
index in \code{"wksd"}, each a single number in \eqn{[0, 1]}. They
have no default, because the source tunes them per network: without
both the measure warns and returns \code{NA}. See
\code{\link{centrality_wksd}}.}

\item{pci_mu}{The \eqn{\mu}{mu} of \code{"mu_pci"}, a single whole
number of at least one, default 1 as in the source. See
\code{\link{centrality_mu_pci}}.}

\item{cycle_alpha}{Discount per edge of a cycle in
\code{"all_cycle_betweenness"}, a single number strictly between 0 and
1, default 0.5. See \code{\link{centrality_all_cycle_betweenness}}.}

\item{transport_beta}{Sensitivity to path length in
\code{"transportation"}, a single finite nonnegative number, default
0.1. See \code{\link{centrality_transportation}}.}

\item{enumeration_limit}{Largest number of search steps taken by the
measures that enumerate all simple paths or cycles
(\code{"all_cycle_betweenness"}, \code{"transportation"},
\code{"path_transfer"}) and of formal concepts built by
\code{"wfca"}, default one million; \code{Inf} removes the
limit. Past it the measure is \code{NA} with a warning.}

\item{lric_quota}{Share of the weight entering a node that a group of
its in-neighbors needs in order to be critical in \code{"lric_max"}, a
single number in \eqn{(0,1]}, default 0.5. See
\code{\link{centrality_lric_max}}.}

\item{lric_path_length}{Largest number of ties of a path of influence in
\code{"lric_max"}: a single whole number of at least one, or
\code{Inf} (default) for all simple paths.}

\item{tpr_alpha}{Jump probability of the trust-PageRank iteration used
by \code{"trust_pagerank"}, a single number strictly between zero and
one, default 0.85 as the source sets it below its equation (7). See
\code{\link{centrality_trust_pagerank}}.}

\item{tpr_k}{Weight of the degree ratio in the trust value of
\code{"trust_pagerank"}, the \eqn{k} of the source's equation (6). The
similarity ratio receives weight \eqn{1-k}. A single number in
\eqn{[0,1]}, default 0.85, the value selected in section 3.3 of the
source. One drops the similarity and zero drops the degree.}

\item{tpr_decay}{Attenuation factor of the similarity recursion used by
\code{"trust_pagerank"}, the \eqn{C} of the source's equation (4); a
single number in \eqn{(0,1]}, default 1 as in the source. \eqn{C}
changes the result. See \code{\link{centrality_trust_pagerank}}.}

\item{tpr_tol}{Convergence tolerance on the largest relative change of
either trust-PageRank recursion, a single positive number, default
\code{1e-14}. The tolerance is relative because the similarities on one
graph span many orders of magnitude. See
\code{\link{centrality_trust_pagerank}}.}

\item{tpr_max_iter}{Iteration bound for both trust-PageRank recursions, a
whole number of at least one, default 1000. Reaching it raises a
\code{cograph_no_converge} warning.}

\item{rsp_beta}{Inverse temperature of the randomized-shortest-paths
model used by \code{"rsp_betweenness"}, a single finite number strictly
above zero, default 0.01, the value \code{NetworkToolbox::rspbc()}
recommends. Small values approach the random-walk limit. Values of 1
and above move the measure towards shortest paths. See
\code{\link{centrality_rsp_betweenness}}.}

\item{rsp_cost}{How an edge weight becomes a traversal cost for
\code{"rsp_betweenness"}: \code{"inverse"} (default) for \eqn{C=1/w},
reading a weight as an affinity, or \code{"weight"} for \eqn{C=w},
reading it as a distance. Both settings give unit cost per arc on a
binary graph. See
\code{\link{centrality_rsp_betweenness}}.}

\item{re_indexes}{Constituent indexes integrated by
\code{"relative_entropy"}, default the source's four distinctiveness
indexes; the vocabulary also holds \code{"n_components"} and
\code{"largest_component"}. See \code{\link{centrality_relative_entropy}}.}

\item{re_negative}{Which of \code{re_indexes} are negative indexes, NULL
for the source's own declarations. See
\code{\link{centrality_relative_entropy}}.}

\item{tna_network}{Logical or NULL. Umbrella switch that forces tna-style
conventions across all measures. \code{NULL} (default) is TRUE when
\code{x} is a \code{tna}, \code{group_tna}, \code{ctna}, \code{ftna}
or \code{atna} object (or a group of these) and FALSE otherwise.
\code{TRUE} applies the tna conventions to any input, setting
\code{invert_weights = TRUE}, \code{loops = FALSE},
\code{diffusion_method = "power_series"} and
\code{transitivity_type = "onnela"}. \code{FALSE} keeps the cograph
defaults for tna inputs as well. An argument passed explicitly always
takes precedence over \code{tna_network}.}

\item{psych_network}{Logical or NULL. Switch for signed psychometric
network conventions. \code{NULL} (default) auto-detects TRUE when a
signed weighted network is evaluated with expected-influence measures.
When \code{TRUE}, normalized expected influence is divided by the maximum
absolute expected-influence value, which keeps its sign and bounds it
between -1 and 1. \code{FALSE} keeps the generic cograph normalization.}

\item{shared_nodes}{Logical. Only used when \code{x} is a group network
object (a Nestimate \code{netobject_group} or a tna group model), which
carries every group on the node set of the whole data. FALSE (default)
computes each group on its own nodes: those that have a tie in the
group (self-loops count) or occur in the group's data, so a member
without ties stays as an isolate. TRUE keeps
the common node set in every group. The result then has one row per node per group, with a
leading \code{group} column.}

\item{...}{Additional arguments (currently unused)}
}
\value{
A base \code{data.frame} with one row per node, in the input's node
order unless \code{sort_by} is given, and the columns:
\itemize{
\item \code{node}: character, the node labels (the index as a string
when the input carried no names)
\item One numeric column per requested measure, with a mode suffix for
the mode-aware measures (e.g., \code{degree_in},
\code{closeness_all}); see \code{\link{list_centralities}} for which
measures carry a suffix. A measure that a tier supplied but that has
no value on this input is an all-\code{NA} column.
}
}
\description{
Computes centrality measures for nodes in a network and returns a tidy
data frame. Accepts matrices, edge-list data frames, igraph objects,
cograph_network, or tna objects.
}
\details{
The following centrality measures are available:
\describe{
\item{degree}{Count of edges (supports mode: in/out/all)}
\item{strength}{Weighted degree (supports mode: in/out/all)}
\item{betweenness}{Shortest path centrality}
\item{closeness}{Inverse distance centrality (supports mode: in/out/all)}
\item{eigenvector}{Influence-based centrality}
\item{pagerank}{Random walk centrality (supports damping and personalization)}
\item{authority}{HITS authority score}
\item{hub}{HITS hub score}
\item{eccentricity}{Maximum distance to other nodes (supports mode).
Distances use the raw edge weights whatever \code{invert_weights}
says, and hop counts with \code{weighted = FALSE}.}
\item{coreness}{K-core membership (supports mode: in/out/all)}
\item{constraint}{Burt's constraint (structural holes)}
\item{transitivity}{Local clustering coefficient (supports multiple types)}
\item{harmonic}{Harmonic centrality, the sum of inverse distances. It
stays finite on disconnected graphs (supports mode: in/out/all)}
\item{diffusion}{Diffusion degree centrality. With
\code{diffusion_method = "kandhway_kuri"} it is the scaled degree of
the node plus the scaled degrees of its neighbors (supports mode:
in/out/all, lambda scaling)}
\item{leverage}{Leverage centrality. Influence over neighbors based on
relative degree differences (supports mode: in/out/all)}
\item{kreach}{K-reach centrality. Number of nodes reachable within
\code{k} steps (supports mode: in/out/all)}
\item{alpha}{Alpha centrality. Influence through paths, attenuated by
length, with a unit exogenous contribution at every node (supports mode:
in/out/all)}
\item{power}{Bonacich power centrality. Influence based on connections
to other influential nodes (supports mode: in/out/all)}
\item{subgraph}{Subgraph centrality. Participation in closed walks,
with shorter walks weighted more heavily}
\item{laplacian}{Laplacian centrality (Qi et al. 2012): the drop in
Laplacian energy when the node leaves, on the weights of a weighted
undirected network. Matches NetworkX}
\item{load}{Load centrality. Share of shortest-path load passing
through the node, with load split evenly at each branching point}
\item{current_flow_closeness}{Information centrality. Closeness based on
electrical current flow (requires a connected graph)}
\item{current_flow_betweenness}{Random-walk betweenness. Betweenness
based on electrical current flow (requires a connected graph)}
\item{voterank}{VoteRank. Influential spreaders selected by iterative
voting. The value is the election order rescaled so that the first
elected node scores 1 and the last scores \eqn{1/n}}
\item{percolation}{Percolation centrality. Shortest-path betweenness
weighted by the node states in \code{states}. With equal states it is
betweenness divided by \eqn{(n-1)(n-2)}}
\item{radiality}{Radiality (Valente and Foreman 1998). Sum of
(diam + 1 - d) over the other nodes, over n - 1.}
\item{lin}{Lin's centrality. Reachable nodes squared divided by sum of
distances.}
\item{decay}{Decay centrality. Sum of \eqn{\delta^d}{delta^d} over all nodes,
the node itself included, with \eqn{\delta}{delta} = \code{decay_parameter}.}
\item{residual_closeness}{Residual closeness (Dangalchev 2006). Sum of
\eqn{1/2^d} over the other nodes.}
\item{dangalchev}{Dangalchev closeness. Same values as
\code{residual_closeness}.}
\item{generalized_closeness}{Generalized closeness. Same formula as
\code{decay}, using \code{decay_parameter}.}
\item{harary}{Harary centrality. Sum of 1/d^2 for all reachable pairs.}
\item{average_distance}{Average distance. Sum of distances to the other
nodes / (n - 1).}
\item{barycenter}{Barycenter centrality. 1 / sum of distances.}
\item{wiener}{Wiener index. Total sum of shortest path distances from node.}
\item{closeness_vitality}{Closeness vitality. Drop in Wiener index when
node removed.}
\item{communicability}{Total communicability. Row sums of matrix exponential.}
\item{communicability_betweenness}{Communicability betweenness. Fraction of
communicability through each node.}
\item{random_walk}{Random walk centrality (Noh and Rieger 2004).
Stationary probability over relaxation time, \eqn{\pi_i / \tau_i}
(requires connected graph).}
\item{stress}{Stress centrality. Number of shortest paths through node.}
\item{flow_betweenness}{Flow betweenness (Freeman, Borgatti and White
1991). Summed loss of maximum flow between other pairs when the node
is removed, as \code{sna::flowbet()}.}
\item{lobby}{Lobby index (Korn et al. 2009): h-index of the neighbors'
degrees.}
\item{entropy}{Graph entropy centrality. Entropy change on node removal.}
\item{semilocal}{Semi-local centrality. Triple-nested neighborhood sum.}
\item{clusterrank}{ClusterRank (Chen et al. 2013). \eqn{10^{-c}} times
the neighbors' (followers') degree + 1 sum.}
\item{bottleneck}{Bottleneck centrality. Count of shortest path trees where
node is critical.}
\item{centroid}{Centroid value (Wuchty and Stadler 2003). Minimum
f(v, u) over the other nodes u.}
\item{mnc}{Maximum Neighborhood Component size (strongly connected
component on directed networks).}
\item{dmnc}{Density of Maximum Neighborhood Component.}
\item{topological_coefficient}{Topological coefficient. Shared neighbor
ratio.}
\item{bridging}{Bridging centrality. Betweenness times bridging
coefficient.}
\item{local_bridging}{Local bridging. (1/degree) times bridging
coefficient.}
\item{effective_size}{Burt's effective size. Degree minus redundancy.}
\item{diversity}{Diversity centrality. Shannon entropy of edge weight
distribution.}
\item{cross_clique}{Cross-clique connectivity. Count of cliques containing
node.}
\item{second_order}{Second-order centrality (Kermarrec et al. 2011).
Standard deviation of the return times to the node of a random walk
made uniform by self-loops, \eqn{\sqrt{2 \sum_i m_{ij} - n(n + 1)}}{
    sqrt(2 sum_i m_ij - n (n + 1))} with \eqn{m_{ij}}{m_ij} the mean
first-passage times, as NetworkX's \code{second_order_centrality()}.
Lower values mark more central nodes. Edge weights are ignored.
Defined on connected undirected networks; otherwise \code{NA} with a
\code{cograph_undefined_measure} warning.}
\item{markov}{Markov centrality. Inverse mean first passage time
(requires connected graph).}
\item{integration}{Integration centrality. Distance-based influence.}
\item{expected}{Expected centrality. Sum of neighbor degrees.}
\item{gilschmidt}{Gil-Schmidt power index. Mean of 1/d over the nodes reached.}
\item{salsa}{SALSA authority scores (directed graphs only).}
\item{leaderrank}{LeaderRank. PageRank with ground node
(directed graphs only).}
\item{participation}{Participation coefficient. Diversity of inter-community
connections (requires \code{membership}).}
\item{within_module_z}{Within-module degree z-score. Intra-community
connectivity (requires \code{membership}).}
\item{gateway}{Gateway coefficient. Inter-community brokerage weighted by
centrality (requires \code{membership}).}
\item{distance_entropy}{Normalized Shannon entropy of a node's
hop-distance profile. It is 1 when the distances are spread evenly
and 0 when all lie at one distance.}
\item{local_dimension}{Growth exponent of the ball around a node
(slope of \eqn{\ln B_i(r)}{ln B_i(r)} on \eqn{\ln r}{ln r}). Lower values mark more
influential nodes.}
\item{local_information_dimension}{Entropy-weighted local dimension
over boxes up to half the node's eccentricity. Higher values mark
more influential nodes.}
\item{neighborhood_connectivity}{Mean degree of a node's neighbors
(average neighbor degree); isolates score 0.}
\item{modularity_vitality}{Drop in modularity when the node is removed
under a fixed partition. Positive values mark community hubs and
negative values mark bridges (requires \code{membership}).}
\item{shapley_game1, shapley_game2, shapley_game3}{Shapley value of the
node in the coverage games of Michalak et al. (2013): one-hop
coverage, \code{shapley_k}-neighbor coverage, and coverage within
\code{shapley_cutoff} hops. Values sum to the node count.}
\item{access_information}{Mean bits needed to reach every other node
along shortest paths without a map. Low values mark well-connected
nodes.}
\item{hide_information}{Mean bits others need to find the node. High
values mark hidden nodes.}
\item{rumor}{Log rumor centrality on the node's BFS tree: log of the
number of spreading orders that could start there.}
\item{community_hub_bridge}{Community size times intra-community
degree plus number of other communities touched times
inter-community degree (requires \code{membership}).}
\item{entropy_variation_degree, entropy_variation_betweenness}{Drop in
the Shannon entropy of the degree (by \code{mode}) or betweenness
distribution when the node is deleted; signed, nats.}
\item{s_shell}{Shell index of the strength-based peeling with
asymmetric topological link weights, exponent \code{s_shell_a}.}
\item{degree_discount, single_discount}{Greedy seed-selection order
under degree discounting (\code{discount_p}) or unit discounting,
scored 1 for the first selected down to 1/n.}
\item{ncvoterank}{VoteRank with voters weighted by normalized
neighborhood coreness (\code{ncvote_theta}); election order scored
like \code{voterank}.}
\item{community_based, comm_centrality, community_mediator}{Links
weighted by the size of the community they reach; Gupta's scaled
intra/inter-degree combination (\code{comm_r}); base-2 entropy of the
link distribution over communities times degree share (all require
\code{membership}).}
\item{local_dimension_fixed, fuzzy_local_dimension,
local_volume_dimension}{Silva-Costa estimator at \code{ld_radius};
slope of the fuzzy ball, where higher values mark more influential
nodes; slope of the degree volume, where lower values mark more
important nodes.}
\item{wvoterank, enrenew, voterank_plus}{Election orders of the
weighted, entropy-based (\code{enrenew_depth}) and degree-weighted
(\code{voterank_lambda}) VoteRank variants, scored like
\code{voterank}.}
\item{node_contraction, node_contraction_improved}{One minus the
agglomeration ratio after contracting the node with its neighbors;
the improved form adds the same score of its edges on the line graph
(\code{contraction_rho}).}
\item{two_way_rw}{Number of node pairs whose most likely two-way
random-walk route passes through the node.}
\item{heatmap}{Farness minus mean neighbor farness. Lower values mark
more central nodes.}
\item{flow_coefficient}{Share of neighbor pairs linked through the
node but not directly.}
\item{local_entropy}{\eqn{-\sum_{j \in N(i)} k_j \ln k_j}{-sum_{j in N(i)} k_j ln k_j}. Lower values
mark more central nodes.}
\item{weighted_h_index}{h-index over topological link weights
\eqn{k_i k_j} repeated \eqn{k_j} times.}
\item{redundancy}{Mean degree of the neighbors inside the ego
network; degree minus effective size.}
\item{weighted_kshell}{k-shell on \eqn{(k^\alpha s^\beta)^{1/(\alpha
    + \beta)}}{(k^alpha s^beta)^{1/(alpha + beta)}} after Garas' weight normalization (\code{wks_alpha},
\code{wks_beta}).}
\item{renewed_coreness}{k-core of the graph after removing links whose
diffusion importance is below \code{renewed_threshold}.}
\item{geodesic_kpath}{Number of shortest paths of length at most
\code{kpath_k} starting at the node.}
\item{local_efficiency}{Global efficiency of the subgraph induced on
the node's neighbors, the node itself removed. This differs from
\code{igraph::local_efficiency()}, which measures the distances
between those neighbors through the rest of the network.}
\item{s_core}{Largest strength threshold whose s-core still contains
the node; the k-core number when weights are absent.}
\item{fragmentation}{Distance-weighted fragmentation of the network
after deleting the node. Higher means a more disruptive removal.}
\item{kpath}{Number of simple paths of length at most
\code{kpath_len} that the node lies on, endpoints included.}
\item{epc}{Edge percolated component: mean size of the node's
component over \code{epc_runs} bond-percolation realizations, as a
share of the network. A Monte Carlo estimate; \code{epc_seed} makes
it reproducible.}
\item{length_scaled_betweenness}{Betweenness with each separated pair
weighted by \eqn{1 / d(s,t)}.}
\item{delta_betweenness}{Betweenness with the pair weight
\eqn{(h(s,t) - 1)^{-\delta}}{(h(s,t) - 1)^{-delta}}
(\code{betweenness_delta}), where \eqn{h(s,t)} is the number of edges
on a shortest path.}
\item{ego_betweenness}{Betweenness inside the node's own ego network.}
\item{delta_closeness}{\eqn{\sum_j d_{ij}^{-\delta} / (n-1)}{sum_j d_{ij}^{-delta} / (n-1)}
(\code{closeness_delta}).}
\item{truss, mdd}{Node truss number (k-2 triangles convention) and
mixed-degree shell threshold (\code{mdd_lambda}). Both use the
simple undirected skeleton; see \code{\link{centrality_truss}}.}
\item{bridging_coefficient, godfather, support}{Reciprocal-degree
ratio, count of unconnected neighbor pairs, and count of
triangle-supported relationships on the simple undirected skeleton.}
\item{volume}{Sum of degrees in the closed \code{volume_radius}-hop
neighborhood on the simple undirected skeleton.}
\item{mcc}{Maximal clique centrality: sum of \eqn{(|C|-1)!} over
incident maximal cliques of size at least two. Costly; see
\code{\link{centrality_mcc}} for isolate and precision conventions.}
\item{diffusion_centrality}{Finite-horizon weighted outgoing walks:
\eqn{\sum_{t=1}^{T}(qA)^t\mathbf{1}}{sum_{t=1}^{T}(qA)^t 1}, with \code{diffusion_q} and
\code{diffusion_steps}. Distinct from diffusion degree.}
\item{dynamical_importance}{Relative spectral-radius loss on vertex
deletion, evaluated by repeated eigendecomposition. Costly; see
\code{\link{centrality_dynamical_importance}} for zero-radius graphs.}
\item{dynamics_sensitive}{Finite-time spreading score including
\code{ds_beta}, \code{ds_mu} and \code{ds_steps}; uses the simple
undirected skeleton.}
\item{malatya}{Sum of focal-to-neighbor degree ratios on the simple
undirected skeleton; the reciprocal of the bridging coefficient
on nonisolated vertices.}
\item{resistance_curvature}{One minus half the incident conductance
times effective-resistance sum. Weighted, componentwise and costly;
see \code{\link{centrality_resistance_curvature}}.}
\item{extended_coreness}{Sum of neighbors' neighborhood coreness;
equivalently the squared simple adjacency times core numbers.}
\item{dkgm}{Gravity with the degree k-shell index as the mass at both
ends, default radius two; see \code{\link{centrality_dkgm}}.}
\item{neighbor_distance}{Benchmark centrality plus its decayed sums
over non-backtracking walks of up to \code{nd_order} steps. See
\code{\link{centrality_neighbor_distance}}.}
\item{ira}{Steady state of a unit resource repeatedly reallocated to
neighbors in proportion to their \code{ira_mass}; conserved, so the
scores of a component sum to its size. Warns
\code{cograph_no_converge} where no steady state exists. See
\code{\link{centrality_ira}}.}
\item{iira}{The same recursion with each share scaled by
\eqn{1-(1-\beta)^{k_i}}{1-(1-beta)^{k_i}} for the \code{iira_beta} spreading rate,
run \code{iira_steps} times.
Decays geometrically, so only the order is meaningful. See
\code{\link{centrality_iira}}.}
\item{lnc}{Local neighbor contribution: the cubed degree times the
binomial own-contribution factor \eqn{(1-1/d_i)^{d_i-1}} times the
neighbors' degree sum over \eqn{n-1}. Parameter-free; raw scores
depend on the whole graph's order. See \code{\link{centrality_lnc}}.}
\item{ked}{KED method: the degree times one plus the normalized
entropy of the neighbors' degrees times \eqn{\exp(K_i/N)}{exp(K_i/N)} for the
neighbor-degree sum \eqn{K_i} and the whole graph's order
\eqn{N}. Parameter-free. See \code{\link{centrality_ked}}.}
\item{hcc}{Hybrid characteristic centrality: the extended degree
\eqn{\delta k_i+(1-\delta)\sum_{j\in N(i)}k_j}{delta k_i+(1-delta)sum_{j in N(i)}k_j} over its maximum,
plus the E-shell peeling round in which the node leaves over the
number of rounds. Raw scores lie in \eqn{[0,2]} and are not
component-local. See \code{\link{centrality_hcc}}.}
\item{ehcc}{Extended hybrid characteristic centrality: the
closed-neighborhood sum of \code{hcc}, the focal node counted once.
See \code{\link{centrality_ehcc}}.}
\item{lhc}{Lhc index: the degree-and-triangle-share influence
\eqn{C(v)=\sum_{u\in\Phi(v)}k_u(1+TP(u))/d^2(uv)}{C(v)=sum_{u in Phi(v)}k_u(1+TP(u))/d^2(uv)} over the ball of
radius \code{lhc_radius}, summed over the open neighborhood. The
triangle share is normalized by \eqn{TNTS=\sum_u NTS(u)}{TNTS=sum_u NTS(u)}, three
times the number of distinct triangles, and is written as zero on a
triangle-free graph. Raw scores are not component-local. See
\code{\link{centrality_lhc}}.}
\item{iec}{Immediate effects centrality: the reciprocal mean length
of the influence sequences that end at a node,
\eqn{(n-1)/\sum_{i\neq j}m_{ij}}{(n-1)/sum_{i!= j}m_{ij}} for the mean first passage times
\eqn{M=(I-Z+EZ_{dg})\mathrm{diag}(1/c)}{M=(I-Z+EZ_{dg})diag(1/c)} of the influence chain
\eqn{W=A/\mathrm{rowSums}(A)}{W=A/rowSums(A)} built with \eqn{a_{ii}=1}.
Direction-sensitive and costly (one eigenproblem and two dense
solves). \code{NA} at every node when the chain is reducible or the
graph has one node. Not the same measure as \code{markov}. See
\code{\link{centrality_iec}}.}
\item{x_nonbacktracking}{X-nonbacktracking centrality: the estimated fall
of the largest nonbacktracking eigenvalue when the node is removed,
\eqn{(\sum_i a_{ci}v^i)^2-\sum_i a_{ci}(v^i)^2}{(sum_i a_ci v^i)^2-sum_i a_ci (v^i)^2}, with \eqn{v^i} the
nonbacktracking centralities of the network without the node and the
eigenvector scaled by \eqn{v^{\top}Pv=1}{v'Pv=1}. Costly (one eigenproblem on the
directed edges per node). \code{NA} where the network without the
node has no principal nonbacktracking eigenvector. See
\code{\link{centrality_x_nonbacktracking}}.}
\item{tec}{Total effects centrality: the stationary vector of the
influence chain \eqn{W=A/\mathrm{rowSums}(A)}{W=A/rowSums(A)} built with \eqn{a_{ii}=1},
the average total effect of a node when the influence process runs
to consensus. Scores sum to one. \code{NA} at every node when the
chain is reducible or the graph has one node. See
\code{\link{centrality_tec}}.}
\item{mec}{Mediative effects centrality: the mean, over the other
nodes \eqn{i} and \eqn{k}, of the probability
\eqn{t_{(k)ij}/t_{(k)jj}}{t_(k)ij/t_(k)jj} that influence from \eqn{i} passes through
the node before reaching \eqn{k}, with
\eqn{T_{(k)}=(I-W_{(k)})^{-1}}{T_(k)=(I-W_(k))^-1} on the same influence chain as
\code{iec}. Direction-sensitive and costly (one dense solve per
node). \code{NA} at every node when the chain is reducible or the
graph has fewer than three nodes. See \code{\link{centrality_mec}}.}
\item{dil}{Degree and importance of lines: the degree plus the share
of each incident line's importance \eqn{I_e=(k_m-p-1)(k_n-p-1)/
    (p/2+1)} that the node's own degree claims,
\eqn{k_i+\sum_{j\in\Gamma_i}I_{e_{ij}}(k_i-1)/(k_i+k_j-2)}{k_i+sum_{j in Gamma_i}I_{e_{ij}}(k_i-1)/(k_i+k_j-2)}, with
\eqn{p} the number of triangles on the line. Two-hop local and
component-local; never below the node's degree. See
\code{\link{centrality_dil}}.}
\item{ink}{Improved neighbors' k-core: the sum over a node's neighbors
of their core numbers raised to \code{ink_alpha},
\eqn{\sum_{j\in J(i)}k_s(j)^{\alpha}}{sum_{j in J(i)}k_s(j)^alpha}. The node's own core number is not
counted and the scores are raw sums. See
\code{\link{centrality_ink}}.}
\item{con}{Common out-neighbor score: the number of out-neighbors a
node shares with every other node,
\eqn{\sum_{v\neq u}\sum_k\min(A_{uk},A_{vk})}{sum_{v!=u} sum_k min(A_uk,A_vk)}. Direction-sensitive;
with \code{weighted = TRUE} weights count as numbers of interactions.
See \code{\link{centrality_con}}.}
\item{emi}{Entropy and mutual information-based centrality: the
base-10 entropy of the neighbors' degree shares plus the mutual
information term
\eqn{\sum_{j\in N_i}\frac{c_{ij}}{d_i+d_j}\log_{10}\frac{d_i+d_j-c_{ij}}{d_i+d_j}}{sum_{j in N_i} c_ij/(d_i+d_j) log10((d_i+d_j-c_ij)/(d_i+d_j))} on common
neighbors. See \code{\link{centrality_emi}}.}
\item{nwrank}{NWRank: the principal eigenvector of the node-link
exchange \eqn{WH}, in which a node shares its score among its links by
the far node's degree and the link betweenness, mixed by
\code{nwrank_alpha}. Scores sum to one. \code{NA} at every node when
the linked nodes form more than one component. See
\code{\link{centrality_nwrank}}.}
\item{biased_random_walk}{Biased random walk centrality: the stationary
distribution of a walk that moves to a neighbor with probability
proportional to \eqn{\alpha f_{deg}+(1-\alpha)f_{nd}}{alpha f_deg+(1-alpha) f_nd} and jumps
uniformly with probability \code{brw_jump}. Scores sum to one. See
\code{\link{centrality_biased_random_walk}}.}
\item{dst}{Dynamical spanning tree centrality: the share of the
network's spanning trees lost when the node is removed,
\eqn{1-t(G\setminus v_i)/t(G)}{1-t(G-v_i)/t(G)}. A cut node scores 1. \code{NA} at every
node of a disconnected network. See \code{\link{centrality_dst}}.}
\item{kdec}{KDEC: the influence \eqn{W(i)W(k)/(n\,e^2)}{W(i)W(k)/(n e^2)} summed over the
nodes one and two steps away, with \eqn{W=k_s d}{W=k_s d} (core number times
degree) and the effective distance \eqn{e_{ij}=1-\log_{10}(1/d_j)}{e_ij=1-log10(1/d_j)},
added along two-step paths. See \code{\link{centrality_kdec}}.}
\item{counting_betweenness}{Counting betweenness: the expected number
of visits a random walk pays the node between its start and its first
arrival at a target, averaged over all ordered pairs. Uses direction,
weights and loops. Costly (one matrix inversion per node). \code{NA}
at every node unless the nodes with both incoming and outgoing ties
are strongly connected. See
\code{\link{centrality_counting_betweenness}}.}
\item{gin}{Global importance of nodes:
\eqn{e^{\alpha k_i/n}\sum_{j\neq i}k_j/d_{ij}}{exp(alpha k_i/n) sum_{j!=i} k_j/d_ij}, the degrees of all other
nodes divided by their distance, times a factor for the node's own
degree. See \code{\link{centrality_gin}}.}
\item{icentr}{Icentr: the sum over the edges of a node's component of
\eqn{2^{-(lev(e)-1)}}{2^-(lev(e)-1)}, with the level of an edge its distance in steps
from the node. See \code{\link{centrality_icentr}}.}
\item{gli}{Global and local information: the mass \eqn{Iks+DC}{Iks+DC} (k-shell
index plus removal round plus degree) of the nodes within
\code{gli_radius} steps, divided by distance, times the exponential
of the node's own share of the total mass. See
\code{\link{centrality_gli}}.}
\item{niem}{Node importance evaluation matrix: a node's efficiency
\eqn{I_i=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j\neq i}1/d_{ij}}{I_i=(1/n) sum_{j!=i} 1/d_ij} times
\eqn{\sum_{j\in N(i)}D_jI_j/\langle k\rangle^2}{sum_{j in N(i)} D_j I_j/<k>^2}, the degree-weighted efficiency of
its neighbors. See \code{\link{centrality_niem}}.}
\item{iksd}{Improved k-shell decomposition: the iteration in which a
node is removed when each iteration takes away only the nodes of
lowest current degree. See \code{\link{centrality_iksd}}.}
\item{density_centrality}{Density centrality:
\eqn{\sum_{1\le d_{ij}\le r}k_i/(\pi d_{ij}^2)}{sum_{1<=d_ij<=r} k_i/(pi d_ij^2)}, with \code{density_radius}
the range \eqn{r}. See
\code{\link{centrality_density_centrality}}.}
\item{wksdn}{Weighted k-shell degree neighborhood: the sum over a
node's ties of \eqn{(ks_i+ks_j)+\lambda(k_i+k_j)}{(ks_i+ks_j)+lambda(k_i+k_j)}, with
\eqn{\lambda}{lambda} the ratio of the total k-shell index to the total
degree. See \code{\link{centrality_wksdn}}.}
\item{mu_pci}{Mu-power community index: the largest \eqn{k} such that
at least \eqn{\mu k}{mu k} nodes within \eqn{\mu}{mu} steps have degree at
least \eqn{k}, with \eqn{\mu}{mu} given by \code{pci_mu}. At 1 it equals
\code{lobby}. See \code{\link{centrality_mu_pci}}.}
\item{all_cycle_betweenness}{All cycle betweenness: the simple cycles
through a node, a cycle of \eqn{k} edges weighing
\eqn{\alpha^{k-2}}{alpha^(k-2)}, with \code{cycle_alpha} the discount. Costly
(enumerates every simple cycle, up to \code{enumeration_limit}
steps). See \code{\link{centrality_all_cycle_betweenness}}.}
\item{transportation}{Transportation centrality: the share of traffic
through a node when traffic between two nodes spreads over all simple
paths with weight \eqn{e^{-\beta C}}{exp(-beta C)}, \eqn{C} the length of the path,
averaged over ordered pairs. Direction-sensitive and costly
(enumerates every simple path). See
\code{\link{centrality_transportation}}.}
\item{path_transfer}{Path-transfer centrality: the entropy, in bits, of
where a flow from the node that never revisits a node and may stop
at every step comes to rest. Direction-sensitive and costly
(enumerates every simple path). See
\code{\link{centrality_path_transfer}}.}
\item{wfca}{Weighted formal concept analysis centrality: the sum of
\eqn{|T|/|P|} over the formal concepts \eqn{(T,P)} of the adjacency
table whose set of common targets \eqn{P} holds the node.
Direction-sensitive and costly (the number of concepts can grow
exponentially; \code{enumeration_limit} applies). See
\code{\link{centrality_wfca}}.}
\item{lric_max}{Long-range interaction centrality, maximal path: the
influence of a node on every other node along the best path, the
influence on one tie being its weight over the smallest critical
group of the target in which the source is pivotal; summed with the
targets weighted by their share of all outgoing weight. Uses
direction and weights. Costly (subset sums over in-neighbors;
\code{enumeration_limit} applies). See
\code{\link{centrality_lric_max}}.}
\item{hybrid}{Hybrid centrality: the sum of a node's ranks on weighted
and unweighted betweenness, closeness and eigenvector centrality, on
degree and on strength, rescaled to run from 0 to 1. \code{NA} at
every node unless the network is undirected and connected. See
\code{\link{centrality_hybrid}}.}
\item{topsis_re}{TOPSIS relative-entropy score: closeness to the
ideal on four weighted indicators (degree, closeness and betweenness
centrality and the improved k-shell index), with relative-entropy
distances to the best and the worst value of each. Between 0 and 1;
a node with a zero indicator scores 0. \code{NA} at every node unless
the network is connected and its nodes are not all alike. See
\code{\link{centrality_topsis_re}}.}
\item{wd}{RMD-weighted degree: the sum over a node's neighbors of the round
in which each is removed by the remaining-minimum-degree
decomposition, divided by the number of rounds. See
\code{\link{centrality_wd}}.}
\item{ewd}{Extended RMD-weighted degree: the sum of \code{wd} over a node's
neighbors. See \code{\link{centrality_ewd}}.}
\item{mlc}{Modified local centrality: \code{semilocal} less twice the sum of
the neighbors' degrees. It can be negative. See
\code{\link{centrality_mlc}}.}
\item{spreading_probability}{Spreading probability centrality: the number
of shortest paths to each node within \code{sp_radius} steps, each
divided by the mean degree once per step. See
\code{\link{centrality_spreading_probability}}.}
\item{profitleader}{ProfitLeader: over a node's neighbors, the degree
mass the node holds apart from the neighbor times the Jaccard
similarity of the two closed neighborhoods. See
\code{\link{centrality_profitleader}}.}
\item{hks}{Hierarchical k-shell centrality: a two-step sum of degree times
the sum of two peeling positions. See \code{\link{centrality_hks}}.}
\item{niccm}{Node importance by the contribution correlation matrix: a
node's efficiency times the efficiency its surroundings hand to it,
shared by the loss each deletion causes. Costly (all distances are
recomputed once per node). See \code{\link{centrality_niccm}}.}
\item{correlation_centrality}{Correlation centrality: the efficiency of
the other nodes, weighted by the number of shortest paths to each and
divided by the distance to the power \code{coc_alpha}. See
\code{\link{centrality_correlation_centrality}}.}
\item{dsc}{Diversity-strength centrality: the mean improved k-shell
index of a node's neighbors, times the entropy of those indices,
times the Jensen-Shannon divergence of the neighbors' shell
distributions. See \code{\link{centrality_dsc}}.}
\item{dsr}{Diversity-strength ranking: the sum of \code{dsc} over the
neighbors. See \code{\link{centrality_dsr}}.}
\item{edsr}{Extended diversity-strength ranking: the sum of \code{dsr}
over the neighbors. See \code{\link{centrality_edsr}}.}
\item{ksgc}{K-shell based gravity centrality: a gravity model with
degree masses, a coefficient that grows with the difference in
k-shell index, and a radius of half the average path length. All 0
when the average path length is below 2. See
\code{\link{centrality_ksgc}}.}
\item{lsc}{Local structural centrality: over the neighbors, the size of
each one's two-step neighborhood and the clustering inside it, mixed
by \code{lsc_alpha}. See \code{\link{centrality_lsc}}.}
\item{classified_neighbors}{Classified neighbors centrality: a degree
in which each neighbor is weighted by its position in the k-shell
decomposition relative to the node (\code{cn_weights}). See
\code{\link{centrality_classified_neighbors}}.}
\item{hybrid_degree}{Hybrid degree centrality: degree and modified
local centrality blended by the spreading probability \code{hc_p},
which must be given; \code{NA} with a warning otherwise. See
\code{\link{centrality_hybrid_degree}}.}
\item{topsis}{TOPSIS centrality: closeness to the ideal node on degree,
closeness and \code{topsis_attribute}, with weights
\code{topsis_weights}. \code{NA} with a warning on a disconnected
network. See \code{\link{centrality_topsis}}.}
\item{all_around}{All-around score: the Euclidean length of degree,
betweenness and k-shell index, each divided by its maximum. See
\code{\link{centrality_all_around}}.}
\item{egm}{Effective gravity model: a gravity model with
entropy-weighted degree masses and a radius of its own for each node.
\code{NA} with a warning on a disconnected network. See
\code{\link{centrality_egm}}.}
\item{gls}{Global and local structure centrality: the squared degree
over \eqn{n - 1}, times the sum over all other nodes of 1.1 to the
power of the number of common neighbors. See
\code{\link{centrality_gls}}.}
\item{ks_if}{K-shell iteration factor: the k-shell index refined by the
iteration of removal within the shell, times the degree, summed over
a node and its neighbors. See \code{\link{centrality_ks_if}}.}
\item{nl}{NL centrality: over the neighbors, the size of each one's
two-step neighborhood plus the importance of the tie to it. See
\code{\link{centrality_nl}}.}
\item{entropy_influence}{Entropy-based social influence (Peng et al.
2017): direct influence from the number of mutual ties and the
entropy of the outgoing weights, plus indirect influence on the nodes
two steps away. Uses direction and weights. See
\code{\link{centrality_entropy_influence}}.}
\item{multi_evidence}{Multi-evidence centrality: degree, betweenness,
efficiency and correlation centrality fused by Dempster's rule;
between -1 and 1. See \code{\link{centrality_multi_evidence}}.}
\item{ksh}{K-shell hybrid method: over the nodes within
\code{ksh_radius} steps, the root of the summed k-shell indices plus
\code{ksh_mu} times the degree, divided by the squared distance. See
\code{\link{centrality_ksh}}.}
\item{eskh}{Extended k-shell hybrid method: the sum of \code{ksh} over
the neighbors. See \code{\link{centrality_eskh}}.}
\item{ikh}{Improved k-shell hybrid method: \code{ksh} with the root of
the product of the k-shell indices and a degree weight that falls
with the distance. See \code{\link{centrality_ikh}}.}
\item{eikh}{Extended improved k-shell hybrid method: the sum of
\code{ikh} over the neighbors. See \code{\link{centrality_eikh}}.}
\item{mcde}{Mixed core, degree and entropy: the k-shell index plus the
degree plus the entropy of the neighbors' shells. See
\code{\link{centrality_mcde}}.}
\item{mcdwe}{Mixed core, degree and weighted entropy: \code{mcde} with
the entropy weighted toward the inner shells. See
\code{\link{centrality_mcdwe}}.}
\item{mcsde}{Mixed core, semi-local degree and entropy: the k-shell
index, \code{semilocal} and the shell entropy, each min-max scaled,
added up. See \code{\link{centrality_mcsde}}.}
\item{mcsdwe}{Mixed core, semi-local degree and weighted entropy:
\code{mcsde} with the weighted entropy. See
\code{\link{centrality_mcsdwe}}.}
\item{lgc}{Laplacian gravity centrality: a gravity model with the
Laplacian centrality as mass and a radius of half the average path
length. All 0 when the average path length is below 2. See
\code{\link{centrality_lgc}}.}
\item{wgravity}{Weighted gravity model: the degree gravity model with a
radius of half the average path length, times the node's entry of
the unit-length leading eigenvector. \code{NA} with a warning when
that eigenvector is not unique. See \code{\link{centrality_wgravity}}.}
\item{asp_centrality}{Average shortest path centrality: the relative
growth of the average distance when the node's ties are removed,
unreachable pairs counted at the diameter. See
\code{\link{centrality_asp_centrality}}.}
\item{wdc}{Weight degree centrality: the number of non-backtracking
two-step walks from a node times its degree to the power
\code{wdc_alpha}. See \code{\link{centrality_wdc}}.}
\item{ewdc}{Extended weight degree centrality: \code{wdc} applied once
more to the \code{wdc} scores; can be negative. See
\code{\link{centrality_ewdc}}.}
\item{mapping_entropy}{Mapping entropy: minus the degree centrality
\eqn{k/(N-1)} of a node times the sum of the logarithms of its
neighbors' degree centralities. See
\code{\link{centrality_mapping_entropy}}.}
\item{dcc}{Degree and clustering coefficient centrality: a degree term
and a two-step clustering term weighted by the entropy weight method.
\code{NA} with a warning on a network without a triangle. See
\code{\link{centrality_dcc}}.}
\item{edge_clustering}{Edge clustering coefficient centrality: the sum
over a node's edges of the triangles on the edge divided by the most
it could be in. See \code{\link{centrality_edge_clustering}}.}
\item{ahp}{Analytic hierarchy process centrality: the weighted shares
of degree, betweenness and closeness (\code{ahp_weights}). \code{NA}
with a warning on a disconnected network. See
\code{\link{centrality_ahp}}.}
\item{semi_ia}{Semi-local iterative algorithm: the steady state of an
eigenvector-like update over the nodes within \code{semi_ia_radius}
steps, weighted by path counts and distance. \code{NA} with a warning
on a disconnected network. See \code{\link{centrality_semi_ia}}.}
\item{synthesize}{Synthesize centrality: normalised degree plus
betweenness, divided by normalised farness. See
\code{\link{centrality_synthesize}}.}
\item{inward_accessibility}{Inward accessibility: the exponential
entropy of the arrivals of self-avoiding walks of \code{ia_steps}
steps, which must be given; \code{NA} with a warning otherwise. See
\code{\link{centrality_inward_accessibility}}.}
\item{improved_entropy}{Improved entropy-based centrality (Ni et al.
2020): the entropies of a node's tie weights and of its neighbors'
degrees, plus an indirect term two steps away. Uses weights;
\code{NA} with a warning on a directed network. See
\code{\link{centrality_improved_entropy}}.}
\item{physarum_spreader}{PhysarumSpreader: the resource a node holds
after \code{physarum_steps} updates of a Physarum flow through a
ground node; uses direction and weights. \code{NA} with a warning
without \code{physarum_steps}. See
\code{\link{centrality_physarum_spreader}}.}
\item{articlerank}{ArticleRank: a PageRank-like score in which a
citing node passes a share set by its number of references
(\code{ar_references}); uses direction. \code{NA} with a warning
where the iteration diverges. See \code{\link{centrality_articlerank}}.}
\item{entropy_gravity}{Entropy-based gravity model: a gravity sum
whose masses combine node H-index, closeness, betweenness and PageRank
with entropy weights. \code{NA} with a warning on a disconnected
network. See \code{\link{centrality_entropy_gravity}}.}
\item{influence_capability}{Influence capability: entropy-weighted sum
of a k-shell position term and a two-step degree sum. See
\code{\link{centrality_influence_capability}}.}
\item{ehc}{Extended H-index centrality: the neighbors' weighted sums of
cumulative neighbor-degree counts (\code{ehc_p}, \code{ehc_r}). See
\code{\link{centrality_ehc}}.}
\item{erm}{Entropy-based ranking measure: neighbor-degree entropies
summed over two-step walks. See \code{\link{centrality_erm}}.}
\item{shell_clustering}{Shell clustering coefficient: a sum over
neighbors of one minus the correlation of their shell vectors plus a
degree term. See \code{\link{centrality_shell_clustering}}.}
\item{ecrm}{Extended cluster coefficient ranking measure: the shell
clustering coefficient summed over two-step walks. See
\code{\link{centrality_ecrm}}.}
\item{weight_neighborhood}{Weight neighborhood centrality: a
benchmark centrality plus the neighbors' values weighted by the
relative importance of the edge. See
\code{\link{centrality_weight_neighborhood}}.}
\item{rcfb}{RCFB: current-flow betweenness with every node in turn as
the source and a common virtual target (\code{rcfb_epsilon}); uses
weights as conductances. \code{NA} with a warning on a directed
network. See \code{\link{centrality_rcfb}}.}
\item{m_centrality}{M-centrality: coreness and a local degree
variation mixed by entropy weights. See
\code{\link{centrality_m_centrality}}.}
\item{wksd}{Weighted k-shell degree neighborhood: sums over the edges
of products of \code{wksd_alpha} degree plus \code{wksd_mu} k-shell
index. \code{NA} with a warning without both weights. See
\code{\link{centrality_wksd}}.}
\item{mapping_entropy_betweenness}{Mapping entropy betweenness: the
node's normalised betweenness times minus the sum of the logarithms of
its neighbors'. See
\code{\link{centrality_mapping_entropy_betweenness}}.}
\item{trust_pagerank}{Trust-PageRank: a damped PageRank whose split of
a node's score among its neighbors is the column-stochastic
trust-value \eqn{T(i,j)=(1-k)s(i,j)/\sum_{l\in N_j}s(j,l)+
    k\,d_i/\sum_{l\in N_j}d_l}{T(i,j)=(1-k)s(i,j)/sum_{l in N_j}s(j,l)+ k d_i/sum_{l in N_j}d_l}, with \eqn{s} the fixed point of SimRank
restricted to the lines of the graph. Scores sum to one when no node
is isolated. \code{NA} at every node of a component that has lines
but no triangle, where the similarity vanishes and the ratio is
undefined. Costly
(two fixed-point recursions over dense matrices). See
\code{\link{centrality_trust_pagerank}}.}
\item{rsp_betweenness}{Simple randomized shortest paths betweenness:
the expected number of visits a node receives over the Boltzmann
distribution on absorbing walks, summed over every ordered
source-target pair. \code{rsp_beta} interpolates between the
random-walk and shortest-path readings. Direction-sensitive,
component-local, and costly (one dense inverse). See
\code{\link{centrality_rsp_betweenness}}.}
\item{relative_entropy}{Normalized geometric mean of several index
distributions, the minimum-relative-entropy integration of
\code{re_indexes}; sums to one. See
\code{\link{centrality_relative_entropy}}.}
\item{mixed_gravity}{Gravity with focal core-number and partner-degree
masses, default radius three.}
\item{extended_mixed_gravity}{Sum of immediate neighbors' raw
mixed gravitational centralities.}
\item{extended_gravity}{Sum of neighbors' raw k-shell gravity scores,
with \code{gravity_radius} applied around each neighbor.}
\item{cda}{Weighted degree and strength, adjusted by Barrat clustering,
plus weighted neighbor contributions; uses \code{cda_alpha}.}
\item{improved_closeness}{Closeness using distances divided by the
number of shortest paths raised to \code{icc_alpha}.}
\item{exogenous}{Contribution to all other nodes' base centrality,
measured by deletion. Selects a base using \code{exogenous_base}.}
\item{global_structure}{Exponential focal coreness times
distance-discounted partner coreness (GSM).}
\item{hybrid_global_structure}{Exponential degree-coreness influences
with an adaptive distance exponent (H-GSM).}
\item{improved_global_structure}{Exponential focal degree with partner
degrees discounted by a global mean-degree distance exponent (IGSM).}
\item{weighted_leaderrank}{Stationary scores with ground-node outgoing
weights determined by original in-degree and \code{wlr_alpha}.}
\item{linerank}{PageRank on the line graph, aggregated at endpoints;
uses \code{damping} and \code{linerank_aggregation}.}
\item{expected_force}{Entropy of onward boundary degrees over
all two-event transmission sequences.}
\item{mcgm}{Multi-characteristics gravity with degree, coreness and
eigenvector masses; default radius two.}
\item{spectralrank}{Outgoing Perron eigenvector with a unit-linked
ground node; \code{sr_prior} supplies optional diagonal information.}
\item{controlrank}{Smallest eigenvalue of each grounded symmetric
row-Laplacian; see \code{\link{centrality_controlrank}}.}
\item{map_equation}{Codelength saving on silencing a node, conditional
on the supplied partition, flow model and coding convention.}
\item{ninl}{Finite neighbor propagation of closed-neighborhood degree
volume; uses \code{ninl_order} and \code{ninl_radius}.}
\item{beta_measure}{BG power shared by successors among predecessors;
\code{beta_direction} selects positive or negative orientation.}
\item{localized_bridging, extended_local_bridging}{Betweenness in
one-hop or two-hop ego networks times the original bridging coefficient.}
\item{modified_expected_force}{Expected Force multiplied by
log degree with the scaling parameter \code{exf_alpha}.}
\item{proximal_betweenness}{First/last shortest-path intermediaries;
uses \code{proximal_variant} on the directed unweighted skeleton.}
\item{x_degree}{Counts four-edge nonbacktracking walks with each node
at the middle, using original neighbor excess degrees.}
\item{coleman_theil}{Concentration of dyadic Burt constraints across
contacts; isolates zero and single-contact nodes one.}
\item{bridging_capital}{Information-walk loss under single-entry deletion;
uses \code{bridging_steps} and \code{bridging_values}.}
\item{random_walk_decay}{Weighted sum of discounted first arrivals
from random walks; uses \code{rwd_decay} and \code{rwd_node_weights}.}
\item{graph_regularization}{Reciprocal diagonal of the inverse
regularized weighted Laplacian, using \code{grc_gamma}.}
\item{adaptive_leaderrank}{Stationary scores with destination weights
determined by original H-indices using \code{alr_h_mode}.}
}
}
\section{Measures without a value on a given input}{
 The community-aware
measures warn and return an all-\code{NA} column when
\code{membership} is missing, and the brokerage roles do the same on an
undirected graph. \code{"relative_entropy"} has no value when one of
its constituent indexes is zero at every node. Named in
\code{measures} or \code{include}, it then raises a
\code{cograph_undefined_index} error. Supplied by a tier, it gives a
\code{cograph_undefined_measure} warning and an all-\code{NA} column,
and the other measures of the tier are still computed.
\code{"flow_betweenness"} requires the igraph package. Without igraph,
naming it raises a \code{cograph_needs_igraph} error, and a tier gives
the same warning and all-\code{NA} column.
}

